there's long been one very very big  problem with Windows laptops the  trackpads  have been bad I mean really really bad  but it's time to take the band-aids off  and put the mouse away windows laptop  makers have been working with Microsoft  to fix the problem in new Windows 10  machines I've been testing this new Dell  XPS 15 for the last week and the  navigation experience is far better Dell  nails one of the essentials space the  glass pad has plenty of room for regular  mousing around and two-finger scrolling  and for once the computer actually  responds to my gestures thanks to a new  precision pad technology and better  Windows drivers  three finger swiping works well and  scrolling is very Swift oh and the rest  of the computer is pretty good too like  tales 13-inch model the 15.6 inch screen  is surrounded by a very thin bezel  making the system closer in size to a  14-inch laptop if not small but it's a  tad shorter than most 15-inch laptops  including apple's retina map of pro the  4k screen is gorgeous but many apps look  pixelated on it since they haven't been  updated for the high resolution screen  and if you care about battery lights  pick the cheaper 1080p version  I got about five-and-a-half hours of  normal use on the 4k screen the 1080p  model should last twice as long Dell  says as a bigger machine the XPS 15  packs some crazy specs my $2,100 model  had a quad-core i7 processor 500  gigabytes of SSD space 16 gigabytes of  RAM and Nvidia graphics I was going to  say that the Dell XPS 15 is now the best  premium Windows machine you can buy then  Microsoft announced the $1,500 surface  book with similar specs stay tuned for  that full review but for now be thankful  that hope is on the way for your faders
 

